State directory
---------------

Product state lives in ~/.omnis-wing/ (POSIX) or
%LOCALAPPDATA%\omnis-wing (Windows).

The pre-rename directory was ~/.hermes/ (POSIX) or
%LOCALAPPDATA%\hermes (Windows). On first run, if the new home does not
already look like agent state, session files are copied from the legacy
directory. The source checkout (hermes-agent/) is not copied. The legacy
directory is not deleted; a pointer file is left behind.

This file, LICENSE, and the README attribution paragraph are the
intended remaining "Hermes" hits besides:

- this NOTICE (legacy path names, upstream URL)
- LICENSE (Nous copyright)
- README.md (one attribution sentence + upstream URL)
- git remote `upstream` → NousResearch/hermes-agent
- wing_constants.py migration (must name ~/.hermes to find it)
- tools/threat_patterns.py and tools/skills_guard.py (legacy attack paths)
- tools/approval.py (legacy `hermes gateway` / `hermes update` commands)
- scripts/release.py contributor emails (historical identities)
- openrouter/hermes3:70b and similar upstream model slugs
